> Preserve the original half-seed educational experiment separately

The old figure used D=7 and a deliberately halved reciprocal seed, even though
the operative integer routine initializes directly at1/d. That educational
experiment is retained by explicitly calling the canonical fixed-update
reciprocal tracer with seed1/14 and six updates. It illustrates e_next=e² in
exact arithmetic, followed by floating rounding limits. It is not presented as
the integer producer’s actual initial state or stopping behavior.

The plotted value is−log10(max(abs(fused residual),10⁻¹⁸)), with a stated
display floor. The residual uses fma(−7,x,1) to reduce cancellation; the actual
update still uses its recorded rounded product/factor. No extra digits or
iterations are invented when floating states stop changing.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/integer_newton_diagnostic.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/division.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::newton_reciprocal_trace(7, 1. / 14., 6);
    std::vector<double> x{0}, digits{-std::log10(std::max(
                                                 std::abs(t.initial_residual),
                                                 1e-18))};
    std::print("| educational completed updates | actual reciprocal | actual fused residual |\n| ---: | " "---: | ---: |\n| 0 | {} | {} |\n",
               t.seed, t.initial_residual);
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.steps.size(); ++i) {
        auto &s = t.steps[i];
        x.push_back(i + 1);
        digits.push_back(-std::log10(std::max(std::abs(s.residual_after), 1e-18)));
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", i + 1, s.after, s.residual_after);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.lines(x, digits, "explicit half-seed", {124, 58, 237}).points(
        x, digits, "", {124, 58, 237}, 5).title("Separate educational reciprocal: D=7, supplied seed1/14").x_label("requested fixed updates").y_label("-log10(max(abs(fused residual), 1e-18))").save_svg("build/integer_newton_diagnostic.svg");
}
```
