> Full-width conversion and correction guards

For N=2⁶⁴−1,D=1, converting N to double rounds it to2⁶⁴. Casting that floating
estimate directly to uint64 is out of range. The corrected producer checks
estimate≥2⁶⁴ and clamps the initial candidate to UINT64_MAX before conversion.
The exact upper test then evaluates(128-bit(q)+1)·D, avoiding the old
uint64(q+1) wrap that could keep the correction loop running incorrectly. Both
guard decisions are captured.

The controls also include maximum dividends divided by2 and3, equal full-width
operands, N<D and the historical zero-divisor sentinel. For N<D the exact
shortcut returns0,N without reciprocal updates. Divisor0 preserves{0,0,0} for
compatibility, with analyzed valid_divisor=false; it is not a mathematical
division result.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/integer_newton_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/division.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto max = std::numeric_limits<std::uint64_t>::max();
    std::vector<std::pair<std::uint64_t, std::uint64_t>> pairs{{max, 1},
                                                               {max, 2},
                                                               {max, 3},
                                                               {max, max},
                                                               {4, 5}, {5, 0}};
    std::vector<std::string> labels{"max/1", "max/2", "max/3", "max/max", "4/5",
                                    "5/0"};
    std::vector<double> corrections;
    std::print("| control | valid divisor | estimate clamped | actual quotient/sentinel | actual " "remainder/sentinel | actual reciprocal updates | exact unit corrections |\n| --- | --- | " "--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < pairs.size(); ++i) {
        auto[n, d] = pairs[i];
        auto t = dm::algorithms::integer_newton_division_trace(n, d);
        auto r = t.analysis;
        corrections.push_back(r.decrements + r.increments);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", labels[i],
                   r.valid_divisor, t.estimate_clamped, r.result.quotient,
                   r.result.remainder, r.reciprocal_updates,
                   r.decrements + r.increments);
    }
    auto p =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(corrections, labels, "unit corrections");
    p.title("Full-width integer Newton controls: actual exact corrections").x_label("original unsigned pair").y_label("actual quotient increments/decrements").save_svg("build/integer_newton_controls.svg");
}
```
